\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  Come down, O Love Divine,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Seek out this soul of mine,
\par And visit it with thy own ardour glowing;
\par O Comforter, draw near,
\par Within my heart appear,
\par And kindle it, your holy flame bestowing.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  O let it freely burn,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Till earthly passions turn
\par To dust and ashes,
\par in its heat consuming;
\par And let your glorious light shine
\par ever on my sight,
\par And clothe me round,
\par the while my path  illuming.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Let holy charity, my outward vesture be,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj And lowliness become my inner clothing;
\par True lowliness of heart,
\par Which takes the humbler part,
\par And o'er its own shortcomings 
\par weeps with loathing.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  And so the yearning strong,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj With which the soul will long,
\par Shall far out pass the power 
\par of human telling;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\fs16\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0\fs24 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj We cannot guess its grace,
\par Till we become the place
\par \pard    Wherein the Holy Spirit 
\par    makes a dwelling.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

